# ResuMatch — environment variables reference
#
# This file is just documentation. The run.bat (Windows) and run.sh
# (Mac/Linux) scripts set the right env vars for you automatically.
# If you deploy to Render/AWS/etc., set these vars in that platform's
# dashboard — see the README for the exact names.
#
# To use a real MySQL (instead of the default H2):
#   1. Set DB_HOST (the rest of the DB_* vars then need to match)
#   2. Set SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=mysql
#   3. The app will switch to MySQL automatically
#
# Without these env vars, the app uses H2 file mode (works out of the box,
# data lives in ./data/resumatch.mv.db, gets reset on every deploy).

# ---- Database (MySQL) ----
# DB_HOST=localhost
# DB_PORT=3306
# DB_NAME=resumatch
# DB_USER=root
# DB_PASS=yourpassword

# ---- Profile selector ----
# SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=mysql
# (do not set this if you want H2; run.bat handles it for you)

# ---- Server ----
# PORT=8080

# ---- Storage ----
# RESUMATCH_STORAGE=/var/data/resumatch/storage

# ---- AI description (optional) ----
# Get a key from https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here
